...)` (push.py lines 360-364). If step 6's transport retry+backoff (0.5s then 2.0s) is applied within that leg, the process sleeps holding the write lock, blocking every other tracker writer for the full backoff budget on each affected pass. The plan does not specify whether the merge-leg backoff sleeps inside or outside the held lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59e138d52bd7ea28","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 6 (merge leg) / src/rebar/_store/push.py lines 287-338, 360-364","norm_id":"n50a0c86399ade925","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A hosted-runner TLS flake during the promisor merge triggers 2-3 in-leg retries while another reconcile/write pass waits on the same store write lock"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the transport-retry sleep for the merge leg is performed OUTSIDE the write_lock (release, sleep, re-acquire per attempt, mirroring how the non-FF outer loop re-enters _recover_non_fast_forward), so backoff never blocks other writers; keep the merge itself under a freshly-acquired lock.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the merge leg resets partial/aborted merge state (e.g. `git merge --abort` or worktree reset) before a transport-retriable re-attempt, so the retry is idempotent and does not act on a dirty index/MERGE_HEAD.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T5b","T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.749,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 6: 'the promisor on-demand fetch that fires inside `git merge` itself ... together with could not fetch ... from promisor remote, because the checkout is a blob:none partial clone'","AC7 asserts the merge 'is retried and then succeeds' but no step describes resetting merge/worktree state between attempts","The push retry is naturally idempotent (re-push same commits); a mid-flight merge failure is NOT obviously idempotent"],"finding":"The plan adds retry to the merge leg (`_merge_remote_under_lock`) where a promisor fetch fails INSIDE `git merge`, but never states whether the worktree/merge state must be reset (e.g. `git merge --abort`) before re-attempting. A `git merge` that fails mid-way on a promisor fetch may leave a partial merge or dirty index, and blindly re-running `git merge` could fail for a spurious reason or corrupt state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5846cb19741eb68e","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 6 (promisor on-demand fetch inside `git merge`) and AC7","norm_id":"nd0dfd942239be275","priority":0.201,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A `git merge` starts applying, hits the promisor fetch over the network, fails with TLS error leaving MERGE_HEAD / partial index; the retry re-invokes `git merge` on already-dirty state and either errors spuriously or produces a bad merge."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a step: before retrying `_merge_remote_under_lock` on a transport-retriable failure, run `git merge --abort` (ignoring 'no merge in progress') to guarantee a clean worktree, and add an AC that proves the retried merge starts from clean state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that PushDeliveryError remains importable as push.PushDeliveryError after the split (re-export fr